Title: Strengthen scope-confinement snapshot to detect in-place overwrites
Created: 2026-06-05
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-06-05T06:24Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context
The scope-confinement guard (ticket 0237, PR #285) snapshots the tree outside
tickets/ before and after each non-install command. Its snapshot() is a path
list only (`find -type f | sort`), so it detects file creation and deletion
but is blind to a command overwriting the CONTENT of an existing file outside
tickets/. The negative control proves teeth against creation only. Flagged as
a non-blocking finding by /verify on PR #285.

## Relevant files
- `tests/test_scopeconfinement.sh` -- snapshot() at ~line 63; negative control at ~line 140

## Actions
1. Extend snapshot() lines with a content signature per file (e.g. `cksum`,
   or size+mtime if hashing every .git file is too slow -- measure first).
2. Extend the negative control: overwrite the content of an existing file
   outside tickets/ (e.g. clobber the seed README) and assert the guard trips.
3. Keep the existing creation-detection control.

## Test
Red step: add the overwrite negative control first -- it must FAIL against the
current path-only snapshot(), proving the gap is real before fixing it.

## Invariants
- All 18 confined commands still pass the guard (no false positives from
  volatile git internals -- keep or refine the existing exclusion list).
- Suite stays hermetic and POSIX-shell only, per existing tests/ conventions.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] snapshot() detects in-place content changes outside tickets/
- [ ] Negative control proves overwrite detection (and creation control kept)
- [ ] make check passes
